{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1395076-gadgets-looking-for-feedback","id":1395076,"title":"Gadgets: Looking for feedback","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-08T07:53:01-07:00","id":1395076,"title":"Gadgets: Looking for feedback","content":"For my game, I've been creating some gadgets to give to my players. My original idea is to give my players a small taste of what Embeds and Exploits are available to them. As well as give my players some access to Embeds and Exploits that mesh better with their better attributes and skills.<br /> <br /> Players:<ul><li>Molly - Her highest attributes are Intelligence, Dexterity, Presence, and Composure. Her highest skills are Investigate, Persuasion, and Subterfuge. Her main tactic is sneaking into locations and fast talking her way out of situations.</li> <li>Alan - His highest attributes are Intelligence, Dexterity, and Resolve. His highest skills are Crafts, Survival, and Subterfuge. His main tactic is trying to outsmart his opponents and computer hacking.</li> <li>Liberty - His highest attributes are Wits, Dexterity, and Stamina. His highest skills are Firearms, Weaponry, and Streetwise.</li> </ul><u><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gadgets</span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Marauder's Map</span></span></b><ul><li>Embed<ul><li>Like I Built It</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>Allows user to know their exact layout of a building and their position within it.</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>A blank piece of parchment that turns into a map when the trigger is said.</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>Saying \u201cI solemnly swear I am up to no good.\u201d</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Wits + Investigation</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>Only works for a specific building.</li> <li>Cannot be used on anything other than buildings.</li> <li>Must read the map for effect to work.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this is to give an extra item for Molly that allows her to use her Investigation skill more. Downside this would have to be for a facility that their handler has scouted out.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vest of Bulletproofness</span></span></b><ul><li>Embed<ul><li>Turn Blade</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>Converts firearm damage from Lethal to Bashing.</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>Covers</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>Putting on.</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Wits + Firearms</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>Only works on firearms.</li> </ul></li> <li>Only switches Lethal to Bashing.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this is to give the players a bit more durability. The downside is my players avoid combat as much as they can so it may be giving me a problem later on when I can't hurt anyone.</i><br /> \u200b</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Break Hammer</span></span></b><ul><li>Embed<ul><li>Raw Materials</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>User smashes a small object with a hammer, destroying it and summon a replacement item of similar size.</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>The hammer appears to be a small rubber mallet.</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>Saying \u201cIt\u2019s hammer time!\u201d</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Strength + Crafts</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>Can only be used on objects that could fit into the palm of a person\u2019s hand</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this is to give Alan a tool that he can use his Craft skill with. Downside, don't know if he'll be able to see the versatility.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Noise Pollution Boombox</span></span></b><ul><li>Embed<ul><li>Interference</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>Spreads exposure across an area, as long as an Angel is within earshot of the music</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>A vintage boombox with a tape deck.</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>Hitting play on a cassette tape. Regardless of cassette tape the sound will cause interference.</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Presence + Subterfuge</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>Only works if Angel is within earshot.</li> </ul></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u200b<br /> <i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this is to help keep the players hidden from Angels if only temporarily. It could be used as an Angel trap if they attract and angel then drop this to keep the angel searching a single area, while they escape. Downside I haven't thrown Angels at my players yet.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Living Recorder Blu-tooth</span></span></b><ul><li>Embed<ul><li>Living Recorder</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>User wearing a Blu-tooth headset records all audio from one scene. Retrieving the Blu-tooth grants the person who holds it can extract 1 Scene from the last 24hrs, all other scenes are lost.</li> <li>Blu-tooth is not the recorder, the recorder is the person wearing the Blu-tooth.</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>A Blue-tooth headset with blinking blue light.</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>Putting Blu-tooth over a person\u2019s ear.</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Intelligence + Computers</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>Can only recover one Scene.</li> <li>Visible on user.</li> <li>Only records audio.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u200b<i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this is to give Alan something he can use with his Intelligence + Computers. Downside, might be too specialized and not useful.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crime Scene DNA Bomb</span></span></b><ul><li>Embed<ul><li>Without a Trace</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>Similar to a Bug Bomb. Activating this device will remove all DNA evidence within the blast radius. The smoke from the bomb will only reach as far as one room.</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>Looks like a can with a pull pin. Similar to Bug Bombs.</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>Pulling the pin from the can.</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Intelligence + Investigation</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>Can only be used once.</li> <li>Only Covers a limited area.</li> <li>Only affects DNA evidence; fingerprints, recordings, witnesses, etc... are unaffected.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this was to give Molly a way to clean a crime scene they create. Downside this might be too specialized, and I haven't done DNA examination yet, so far eye witness testimony and bullet forensics.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Groucho Glasses</span></span></b><ul><li>Embed<ul><li>Occam\u2019s Razor</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>Putting on the Groucho Glasses will make people perceive the wearer as an oddball to cover up any compromise that may have occurred. The glasses act as a +2 to Cover before a User\u2019s Cover is actually damaged.</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>A pair of black rimmed glasses with a fake nose and mustache attached.</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>Putting on the glasses and saying a Groucho Marx quote activates the device.</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Presence + Persuasion</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>The glasses are very obviously weird.</li> </ul></li> </ul><i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this was to give a weird gadget they might have fun with. Downside I haven't damaged anyone's cover yet, might not be the best.</i><br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exploited Gadgets</span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">False Idol</span></span></b><ul><li>Exploit<ul><li>Sermon</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>The user with the False Idol is able to create a cult around it. The rules to do so follow the rules for Sermon.</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>A twisted golden statue with organic components that bleed real blood.</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>A drop of blood in the idol\u2019s mouth.</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Manipulation + Occult</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>Cultists are only loyal to the False Idol statue. Demon can manipulate them, but those affected will never believe that the False Idol represents the Demon.</li> <li>Cult has a higher chance to be corrupted by zealots within itself.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this was to delve a bit more into cults, which I haven't done much yet. Downside, my players aren't keen on dominating mortals.</i>\u200b</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Body-Buzzer</span></span></b><ul><li>Exploit<ul><li>Possession</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>The demon has the Body buzzer in the palm of their hand. Shaking the hand of an individual will allow the demon to possess the target for 4 hours.</li> <li>Demon\u2019s body disappears and the Body-buzzer is switched to the target\u2019s hand.</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>A small metal joybuzzer that can be hidden in the palm of one\u2019s hand. The button is replaced with a bloodshot eye ball.</li> <li>Joybuzzer is hide-able, but easily identified as occult.</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>Pressing the buzzer into another person\u2019s hand.</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Presence + Subterfuge</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>Only lasts 4 hours.</li> <li>The buzzer must remain in the possessed person\u2019s hand. Removing it ends the effect.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u200b<i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this is to give my players another way to get an alternate identity. Downside, I don't think this has<br /> much of a downside, the demon has to keep the buzzer hidden in their right hand. Opening their hand to manipulate things risks exposure.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hel-Gun</span></span></b><ul><li>Exploit<ul><li>Hellfire</li> </ul></li> <li>Effect<ul><li>The gun\u2019s profile does Aggravated damage instead of Lethal.</li> </ul></li> <li>Appearance<ul><li>The Hel-Gun looks demonic, blood red metal with plumes of flame that emanates from the center of the gun. When a shot, these plumes of fire jet out in a showy display.</li> </ul></li> <li>Trigger<ul><li>Pulling the trigger of the gun.</li> </ul></li> <li>Activation Roll<ul><li>Intelligence + Firearms</li> </ul></li> <li>Limitations<ul><li>The Hel-Gun eats through its Aether reserve faster than normal Exploited gadgets, requiring Aether whenever its ammo runs out.</li> <li>Higher ammo capacity guns have more limited capacity.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <i>\u200bGM Notes: My goal for this was to give everyone, but Liberty a better gun to fight Angels. Downside, I'm not sure if the limitations will keep the players from using these in every combat encounter. Additionally the downside of it being a loud weapon might keep my stealthy players from using them.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","user":"DontEatRawHagis","date":".  Formating 06-08-2020, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T15:21:16-07:00","id":1396078,"title":"","content":"Here is what I came up with. These are just my opinions and please take them or leave them as you wish. <br /> <br /> <b>Overall, these look great. </b><br /> <br /> <b>Marauder's Map</b><br /> <br /> I would limit this to the person who activates it. Yes, it would take away from the \u2018coolness\u2019 of it. Alternatively, maybe spend a point of Aether to have anyone use it who is viewing the map. There is a comparable Angel power called \u2018Hallowed Ground\u2019 I think. That one limits it to the original building construction. Example: Someone builds a 3 bedroom house and 3 years later adds on another bedroom. That extra bedroom would not be visible on the map.<br /> <br /> <b>Vest of Bulletproofness</b><br /> I like this one as-is.<br /> <b>Break Hammer</b><br /> <br /> This definitely depends on the imagination of the player as you pointed out. You might have someone demonstrate it if it is \u2018found\u2019. <br /> <br /> <b>Noise Pollution Boombox</b><br /> This is a cool gadget. Love it.<br /> <br /> <b>Living Recorder Blu-tooth</b><br /> I would give a little more usage here. Perhaps extracts audio one scene per 2 successes or something. <br /> <br /> <b>Crime Scene DNA Bomb</b><br /> <br /> I would set a limit here in the size. One room only but would expand it to do everything that Without a Trace does. Rename it \u201cCrime Scene Scrub Bomb\u201d or something.<br /> <br /> <b>Groucho Glasses</b><br /> Be careful with this one as it could throw things out of whack in regard to compromise rolls. It might be good for low-level demons. Higher level who can manipulate compromise rolls by different means (4 minutes ago, etc.) would not find it as useful.<br /> <br /> <b>False Idol</b><br /> I\u2019ve never had much luck with playing or ST\u2019ing games where you have cultists. It could be cool to give to a stigmatic who can use it against the players.<br /> <br /> <b>Body-Buzzer</b><br /> I like this one. It is similar to the \u201cTranslocation\u201d Numina for Angels. You could add a failure that they \u2018swap bodies\u2019. That could be fun for a few hours.<br /> <br /> <b>Hel-Gun</b><br /> Looking at what does Aggravated damage, be careful with this one. If I read your limitations correctly, you spend an Aether when the clip runs out. I would change that to \u201c1 Aether to load the gun and 1 Aether per scene.\u201d Fighting Angels can\u2019t be TOO easy after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}